  "_id": "6682bd7cba0e94a3c4025cf4",
  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "Two resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>Ω</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mi>Ω</mi></math> are connected in series with a battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and negligible internal resistance. A voltmeter is used to measure voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mi>Ω</mi></math> resistance, which gives reading as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The resistance of voltmeter must be _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ω</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "200",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cafbf6da-e5ec-482e-a2ed-50d4bf93dc50.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 215px;\"/></p><p>Voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p>Therefore, current through the battery, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>200</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, equivalent resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo> </mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo> </mo><mn>100</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>For voltmeter, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>200</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>200</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
